#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""OptMem: a permanent, append-only memory for AI agents.

  {memo} init [--memory-dir PATH]  initialize user and global memories.
  {memo} wake [part]              read user, global, and current workspace.
  {memo} note --scope SCOPE "..."  record one memory in an explicit scope.
  {memo} nap [id "..."]   do the pending compressions.
  {memo} recall <regex>   search every memory ever recorded.
  {memo} zoom <lo>-<hi>   open a tree node: its two halves.
  {memo} forget <lo>-<hi> drop a bad summary; nap rebuilds it.
  {memo} config [NAME=N]  show this memory's sizes, or change one.
  {memo} import <file>    bulk-load dated memories (bootstrap only).

Scopes: user, global, workspace. note/nap/zoom/forget/import require --scope.
Workspace defaults to the current directory.
Use --workspace PATH to override it, --memory-dir PATH to override the root.
The root is $MEMORY_DIR, the saved init path, or ~/.optmem/memory.
wake/recall without --scope read only user, global, and the current workspace.
See github.com/VictorTaelin/OptMem.
"""

